## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical guardrail implementation and rollback in Azure, focusing on private endpoints and storage exposure controls.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy initiatives
- Private Endpoint and Private DNS for SQL
- Storage account publicNetworkAccess controls
- Post-deploy validation and rapid rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Post-deploy validation sketch (Node.js)
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");
const { StorageManagementClient } = require("@azure/arm-storage");
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const subscriptionId = "<sub-id>";
const client = new StorageManagementClient(credential, subscriptionId);
async function checkStoragePublicAccess(rg, name) {
  const acc = await client.storageAccounts.getProperties(rg, name);
  return acc?.properties?.networkAcls?.publicNetworkAccess !== "Enabled";
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this in a dev environment before production rollout?
- What logs/alerts would you configure to catch violations early, and how would you automate rollback if the last-good template isn’t found?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to translate a threat model into Azure‑native controls, tying identity lifecycle (PIM/JIT, minimal RBAC) to network segmentation (Private Endpoints, NSGs) and automated IR (Defender for Cloud, Sentinel) with verifiable rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Just‑In‑Time (PIM) and ephemeral workload identities
- Least‑privilege RBAC scoped to resources
- Private Endpoints and network segmentation (NSGs, subnets)
- Defender for Cloud and Azure Sentinel integration
- Automated containment playbooks and rollback procedures

## Code Example

```javascript
// PIM‑like pseudo‑API to request ephemeral access (illustrative)
async function requestEphemeralAccess(role, resourceId) {
  const approval = await pim.request({ role, resourceId, ttlSeconds: 3600 });
  if (!approval.approved) throw new Error('PIM approval failed');
  return approval.credentials;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rollback plan without impacting production?
- What metrics and alerts would validate containment efficacy during an incident?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical use of CMK with storage in Azure and policy-driven governance across subscriptions; includes rollout, rollback, and testing.

## Key Concepts
- CMK in Azure Key Vault
- Azure Policy with DeployIfNotExists/AuditIfNotExists
- Key rotation, backups, and compliance reporting
- Per-subscription scoping and rollout testing

## Code Example
```json
{
  "policyName": "StorageAccounts-CMKBackedEncryption",
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
        {"field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/encryption.keySource", "notEquals": "Microsoft.KeyVault"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  },
  "parameters": {
    "keyVault": {"type": "String"}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle existing storage accounts that already use platform-managed keys?
- What monitoring/auditing would you add to ensure ongoing CMK compliance?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CMK usage, Key Vault integration, identity access, policy enforcement, and rollback planning at beginner level.

## Key Concepts
- Customer-managed keys (CMK) for storage at rest
- Azure Key Vault with managed identities
- Storage Account encryption properties and keyVaultProperties
- Azure Policy to require CMK on new storage accounts
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// ARM-like snippet illustrating CMK encryption on a storage account
{
  "type": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts",
  "name": "[storageAccountName]",
  "apiVersion": "2023-01-01",
  "location": "[resourceGroup().location]",
  "properties": {
    "encryption": {
      "keySource": "Microsoft.KeyVault",
      "keyVaultProperties": {
        "keyName": "<cmk-name>",
        "keyVaultUri": "https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net/"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate CMK policy compliance in CI/CD? 
- How would you handle CMK rotation without downtime?

